Error [E0209]: `consume` takes `msg`, but `msg` is used again later
  --> unmarked_take_argument_reused_after_branch_teaches_copy.jet:11:17
    |
 11 |         consume(msg)
    |                 ^^^
  --> unmarked_take_argument_reused_after_branch_teaches_copy.jet:13:11
    |
 13 |     print(msg)
    |           ^^^ `msg` is used again here
 Why: `consume` takes ownership of this argument; an unmarked argument moves only at its name's last use, and this is not the last use of `msg`
 Fix: Write `msg.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `msg`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `msg`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209
